I used the config file from Redhat.  It may be out of date for the
alpha on the SIS.

(mic:9) fgrep -i sis kernel-2.4.18-i686.config kernel-2.4.18-alpha.config 
kernel-2.4.18-i686.config:CONFIG_SIS900=m
