Well, According to Apple. They can put out 630 GFLOPs
in a 42U rack as opposed to the CS20 which claims
140 GFLOPs in the same space. I find very hard to believe
Apple's numbers. When 'real' HPTC guys get their hands
the hardware we'll find out exactly how fast they are
without the 'spin'. Also in the x86 world. 

http://www.angstrommicro.com/products/racer500_quad.htm

Quad processor K7 in 1U. Though the description skirts
around my question of whether it's a true 4 way SMP system
or a pair of 2 ways stuffed into a 1U. No mention of
GFLOPS.

Anyways, Apple is singing to the choir 90% so I really
wouldnt worry about their claims much or give them
much weight. 

