household word, even in the Unix community. Compaq never managed to
generate any kind of "mind-share" for Alpha and consequently they never
managed to sell any. 

It's very sad, but very true.

And by the way, I haven't heard anybody mention the Netra. It's Sun's 1u
SPARC box that's been out for over a year.

And in response to someone's comment about "preaching to the choir."
As I understand things - that statement is very true. Interestingly, Apple
didn't/doesn't anticipate any "conflict/competition" between other vendors
products and the Xserv.  They seem to be genuinely surprised at the
attention its getting.

-- 
