I recently bought an AlphaStation 200 4/233.  I loaded
RH 7.1 on it, successfully.  When I boot the computer,
it brings me to the graphical login screen.  My
keyboard (generic DEC 101 key) and my mouse (standard
ps2) are not recognized by Linux.  The SRM console
takes input from my keyboard, so I know it is working
fine (plus, I used it to type things in with during
the install).

How should I have things set up so that I can still
use the keyboard and mouse?  I am new to Alpha's, so
it might be an easily preventable problem that I am
just not aware of.

I am using the standard Alpha with a Matrox Millenium
4mb graphics card and a Creative Labs SB 16pnp.

Any help would be greatly appreciated.

Jim Gross

