> 
> I am familiar with building the kernel on an intel platform. The thing
> that I am stuck on is the equivalent make commands to:
> 
> make bzImage

This is x86 only platform specific command.  _Everywhere_ else
'make boot' is what you need.  Have a peek into a top Makefile
and arch/*/boot/Makefile files.

As a matter of fact 'make boot' works on x86 too but it is equivalent
to 'make zImage' (a default target in a corresponding Makefile).

> make install

You may always run /sbin/installkernel, or similar script which you
can edit to a taste yourself, or just copy what you want/need
after 'make modules_install'.

  Michal




