storri@ameritech.net said:
> I rebuilt 2.4.18 and copied it to /boot. I made my entry to aboot.conf
> similar to yours. Now the boot get to the following line and does
> nothing: 

Make sure the file names are the same everywhere. Notice in my example
that I used the name vmlinuz-2.4.18 (see the "z" there?) for the
vmlinux.gz that I copied from the 2.4.18 build area.

Also, make sure the root=/dev/sdaX is correct for your machine.
Look at the values that were placed there by the installer for your
distribution.

Note that in me example, the entry was:

  5:1/vmlinuz-2.4.18 root=/dev/sda2

The "5" is the entry number for selecting with the -fl option.

The "1" is the partition number, and replaces the /boot on my system.
Check the other entries for the distribution installed kernels to
get the partition number right. Then note that the file name is
/vmlinuz-2.4.18. Get the name right, and note that the "1" probably
replaces a "/boot" on some, perhaps most, installations.

Finally, note the "root=/dev/sda2" that points to the root partition.
In my case, and probably the typical case, this is different from the
boot partition. Again, look at other lines in your aboot.conf file
