On Fri, May 17, 2002 at 10:54:48PM -0500, Stephen Torri wrote:
> 
> I rebuilt 2.4.18 and copied it to /boot. I made my entry to aboot.conf
> similar to yours.

Keep in mind that full file names in 'aboot.conf' are relative to a
top of a partition on which your kernels (and 'aboot.conf') reside
and not to the top of your whole file system when eventually everything
is mounted.  These two may, or may not, coincide.  It is, actually,
usually a good idea if they don't with /boot beeing a small and "simple"
partition.

> Now the boot get to the following line and does
> nothing:
> 
> aboot: starting kernel vmlinuz-2.4.18 with arguments root=/dev/sda2
> 
> I cannot see activity.

Maybe you could start with precompiled kernels?  Probably something
fishy in your configuration.  For booting with SRM console this either
should be a "generic" kernel or SRM support should be explicitely set.

   Michal




