I got my Oxygen VX1 repaired and made a go at installing it and
XFree86-4.2.0-7 from the RedHat rawhide area on my otherwise stock
RedHat 7.1 system. It is still soon, but it appears to be working
nicely. So far:-) Here's what I did:

I downloaded these RPMS from the rawhide area. Note that some are
RPMS that XFree depends on, and not XFree86 RPMS per se...

freetype-2.0.9-2.alpha.rpm
Glide3-20010520-13.alpha.rpm
go.sh
hwdata-0.14-1.noarch.rpm
kudzu-0.99.52-1.alpha.rpm
Xconfigurator-4.10.7-1.alpha.rpm
XFree86-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-75dpi-fonts-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-base-fonts-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-devel-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-doc-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-font-utils-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-libs-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-tools-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-truetype-fonts-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-twm-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-xdm-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-xf86cfg-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
XFree86-xfs-4.2.0-7.alpha.rpm
xinitrc-3.22-1.noarch.rpm

I ran "rpm -Uvh ..." to verify that the only unconnected dependency is
for the kernel-dri-4.2.0, which is not provided by any kernel rpms. I
then installed with "rpm -Uvh --nodeps ...".

I checked that I had no lingering XFree86-4.0.3 or XFree85-3.3.6 rpms
(I did, the 3DLabs, S3 and Mach64 servers) then configured with Xconfigurator.

Thanks RedHat for having a rawhide area:-)
