To the list:

I have been having some peculiar behavior from my KDE desktop in root
mode, very bothersome and getting worse. While going thru my
/var/log/messages file i noticed that most of the events are in crono
sequence .. but once in a while something is logged 2 or 3 minutes
before the event preceding it. Then back to normal for a while, then
another out-of-sequence msg.  

Occasionally the system clock on my pws500a/u loses a couple minutes, or
an hour or half a day, for no discernable reason.

Most of my clock problems are caused by switching over to AlphaBios, or
the SRM clock getting whacked by Tru64 on startup. This one is different
...

Has anyone experienced anything similar?  

TIA

jon norstog




