I can say for certain, that X11 was not designed with the idea of 
the system time changing out from underneath it.  On any system 
running X11, one must take good measures to ensure that the clock 
does not get changed drastically.  I strongly recommend keeping 
the clock syncronized to the second as accurately as possible 
while X is running, or if time changes in excess of 2-3 seconds 
are likely to occur, to instead shut down X, change the time and 
restart X.

Until changes occur in X11 that solve this problem, then there is 
no simple solution.


