Hello!

I have already posted this question into comp.os.linux.alpha but the real
point is I have no idea what may be happening.

I have recently updated a ruffian system from RH6.2 into RH7.1 making use
of the ruffian-milo.img available from:
gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/TESTING/ruffian-milo.img
I dd'ed it into a floppy and the actualization from the CD's was made
without problems in text mode.

However, just before the end of the proccess, I followed the instructions
in the RH-Instal-Guide and dd'ed the ruffian image I had used into my DOS
boot partition (/dev/sda1).

Well, from that point on, it became completely imposible to boot the machine
from that partition. The strange thing is that it boots without problem
from the same milo and ldmilo.exe files (at least its checksums are equal)
provided that they are in a floppy.

I have tried to undo the patch which was published in this list last year
without succes (in booting from /dev/sda1, no problems with /dev/fd0).

Another funny point is that it gives no error messages at all. If I introdu=
ce
a bad path, it complains it does not find the loader; if I introduce the
correct one, the system makes nothing. In one of my last trials I have
tried the "Run a program" option. In such situation, there is the following
error message:
c:ldmilo.exe =3D=3D> "Not enough memory to load program"

Some data:
ARCS BIOS 1.3.061 (SN 3010000.510A46)
APC 164UX/BX

So my plea is just to know whether anybody else has had a similar problem
and has been able to solve it. If not, is it possible to downgrade the
milo into the one I had previously? I have lost it, but I remember it
was compiled against 2.0.30. Where can I found milo and ldmilo.exe from
that time? and, are they able to load 2.4.x kernels?

Thank you very much for your time to read this mail.
