Basicly a UP1000 with an embedded EV6 (sometimes EV67) CPU running at 600Mhz
plus it
has onboard sound and ethernet. 1 AGP slot and 3 PCI available. The sound
drivers are fully supported by ALSA since one of the lead developers has one
along with a UP2K. The southbridge also supports UDMA 66 and is quite fast. I'm
not sure whether the ethernet was DEC or Intel based. Either way they're both
good performers. Makes an excellent workstation. You really don't need SCSI with
the UDMA 66, especially after it's been tweaked.

Did I sell anyone on it? ;-)

